NEARS-2413 QA (iOS, iPhone 17e simulator) — regression_bugs finding, NOT this ticket's defect.
Live render-tree excerpt (ext.flutter.debugDumpRenderTree) — category_screen.dart grid, category_id=6.

Item "Birds Eye Frozen Meall" (unrated -> "NEW" badge branch):
  RenderParagraph (product-name Flexible)
    constraints: BoxConstraints(0.0<=w<=116.0, 0.0<=h<=12.2)
    size: Size(116.0, 12.2)
    text: "Birds Eye Frozen Meall" (PublicSans SemiBold 15.0, weight 600)

Live-measured natural height for the SAME text/style (via VM-Service evaluate,
TextPainter constructed identically to the shipped widget test's own
naturalOneLineHeight() helper):
  natural 1-line height @ width 116 = 18.0
  natural 2-line height @ width 116 = 36.0 (this name genuinely wraps to 2 lines)
  observed live box height           = 12.2   <-- BELOW even 1 natural line

Root cause (isolated via sibling-offset diffing in the same dump):
  Sibling "unit" row height is identical (21.0) in both cases.
  Sibling rating-Row height (rated items):        18.0
  Sibling NBadge "NEW"-pill height (unrated items): 23.0   <-- 5.0pt taller
  Column mainAxisSize:min gives the name Flexible whatever height remains after
  fixed siblings inside the SAME Expanded(flex:4) budget (mainAxisExtent 273/298,
  unchanged by this analysis regardless of screen). The NBadge's extra 5.0pt is
  taken directly out of the name's budget: 17.2 (rated) - 5.0 = 12.2 (unrated).
  This exactly matches the observed delta (17.2 vs 12.2).

Cross-check confirming this is PRE-EXISTING / NOT introduced by this ticket's diff:
  Same live app, same session, navigated to store_screen.dart's own grid
  (store_id=2, "Fresh Mart Grocery", byte-identical mainAxisExtent:273/298 +
  crossAxisCount:2/3 to category_screen.dart's post-fix values, confirmed via
  git diff/read of store_catalog_states.dart:82-83 / store_screen.dart:2001-2015).
  IDENTICAL squeeze reproduced on REAL unrated seed items there too:
    "QA OOS Fixture — Sparkling Water 500ml" -> box height 12.2
    "Barilla Orzo Pasta"                     -> box height 12.2
  vs rated/short items on the same grid:
    "Potatoes" / "Carrots" / "Lemon Soda 1.5L" / "Navel Oranges" / "Salted Pretzels"
    -> box height 17.2 (all short enough that even the un-squeezed budget is
       sufficient, single line, no visible truncation)

Repro items observed squeezed (category_screen.dart, live, category_id=6):
  "Birds Eye Frozen Meall"  (22 chars) -> 12.2 (natural 1-line=18.0, 2-line=36.0)
  "Great Value Vegetable"   (truncated in capture, item name continues)
  "Marie Frozen Meal"                  -> 12.2
  "Brown Bread"                        -> 12.2

Root cause lives entirely in item_widget.dart's NBadge ("New" pill) sizing —
a file this ticket explicitly keeps read-only/out-of-scope (per the ticket's
own already-blessed precedent for the sibling rating-Row horizontal-overflow
finding). Present identically, byte-for-byte, on the already-shipped
store_screen.dart grid using the SAME shared ItemWidget + SAME mainAxisExtent
values -> this ticket's fix correctly mirrors its sibling; it inherits, but
does not introduce, this residual squeeze.

Recommended fix-forward (not this ticket): either shrink NBadge's own
padding/decoration to <= the rating-Row's height (18.0), or bump the shared
mainAxisExtent value (273/298, both screens) enough to absorb the 5.0pt
delta with margin for 2-line names. Either requires touching item_widget.dart
and/or the shared geometry constant used by BOTH screens - out of scope for a
single-file, sibling-parity ticket.
